{"title":"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>palindrome</i> is a positive integer that is the same when read forwards or backwards. For example, three palindromes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ad7692f5d86be790209a56a68c2a3488235054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/5399794b44034434d41f9fc49e73f4966feb8e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7739377$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Parts\">Parts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Parts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a\" title=\"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4a\">2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4a</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4b&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4b (page does not exist)\">2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4b</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2